# Color Usage Rules for Next.js

## 🎨 Approved Modus Colors (9 Total)

### ✅ ONLY Use These Modus CSS Variables

**Base Colors (5 total):**

```css
/* Light Theme → Dark Theme */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)     /* #fff → #000 */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-100)      /* #f1f1f6 → #252a2e */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)      /* #cbcdd6 → #464b52 */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-300)      /* #b7b9c3 → #353a40 */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)  /* #171c1e → #cbcdd6 */
```

**Semantic Colors (4 total - same in both themes):**

```css
var(--modus-wc-color-info)          /* #0063a3 */
var(--modus-wc-color-success)       /* #1e8a44 */
var(--modus-wc-color-error)         /* #da212c */
var(--modus-wc-color-warning)       /* #fbad26 */
```

**Note:** `primary`, `secondary`, `tertiary`, and `danger` are component-specific color props that map to these CSS variables internally.

### 🎯 Next.js Color Usage Patterns

#### Correct Implementation with Inline Styles:

```tsx
export default function Component() {
  return (
    <div
      className="component"
      style={{
        backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)",
        border: "1px solid var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)",
        color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)",
      }}
    >
      <ModusWcButton color="primary">Primary Button</ModusWcButton>
      <ModusWcButton color="secondary">Secondary Button</ModusWcButton>
      <ModusWcButton color="warning">Warning Button</ModusWcButton>
      <ModusWcButton color="danger">Danger Button</ModusWcButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### Correct Implementation with CSS Modules:

```tsx
// Component.tsx
import styles from "./Component.module.css";

export default function Component() {
  return (
    <div className={styles.component}>
      <ModusWcButton color="primary">Primary Button</ModusWcButton>
      <ModusWcButton color="secondary">Secondary Button</ModusWcButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```css
/* Component.module.css */
.component {
  background-color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-page);
  border: 1px solid var(--modus-wc-color-base-200);
  color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-content);
}

.component:hover {
  background-color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-100);
}
```

## 🚫 NEVER Use These Colors

### ❌ Hardcoded Hex Values

```css
/* FORBIDDEN - Will be flagged by linter */
color: #fff;
background: #f1f1f6;
border-color: #0063a3;
background-color: #da212c;
```

### ❌ Hardcoded RGB/RGBA Values

```css
/* FORBIDDEN - Will be flagged by linter */
color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
background: rgba(241, 241, 246, 0.8);
border-color: rgb(0, 99, 163);
```

### ❌ Tailwind Color Classes

```css
/* FORBIDDEN - Will be flagged by linter */
.text-red-500 .bg-blue-400 .border-gray-300 .text-green-600 .bg-slate-100;
```

### ❌ Non-Modus CSS Variables

```css
/* FORBIDDEN - These don't exist in our system */
var(--secondary)
var(--tertiary)
var(--danger)  /* Use --modus-wc-color-error instead */
var(--border)
var(--text-primary)
var(--bg-secondary)
```

### ❌ Custom Color Variables

```css
/* FORBIDDEN - Don't create your own color variables */
:root {
  --my-blue: #0063a3;
  --custom-gray: #f1f1f6;
  --app-red: #da212c;
}
```

