## 🛡️ Pre-commit Color Linting for Next.js

### Automatic Detection

The project automatically detects and prevents:

- Hardcoded Modus hex values (`#fff`, `#f1f1f6`, etc.)
- Tailwind color classes (`red-500`, `bg-blue-400`, etc.)
- RGB/RGBA color values
- Non-Modus CSS variables

### Manual Check

```bash
npm run lint:colors
```

### Next.js Integration

The color checking script (`scripts/check-modus-colors.js`) is specifically configured for Next.js projects:

- **File Patterns**: Checks `app/**/*.{tsx,ts,js,css,scss}`, `components/**/*.{tsx,ts,js,css,scss}`, `src/**/*.{tsx,ts,js,css,scss}`, `styles/**/*.{css,scss}`
- **Husky Integration**: Pre-commit hook runs `lint-staged` which executes color checking
- **ES Module Support**: Uses `"type": "module"` in `package.json` for modern JavaScript
- **Next.js Specific**: Optimized for Next.js 15 with React 19 and App Router structure

### Common Violations & Fixes

#### ❌ Violation:

```css
.header {
  background-color: #f1f1f6;
  color: #171c1e;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #cbcdd6;
}
```

#### ✅ Correct:

```css
.header {
  background-color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-100);
  color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-content);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--modus-wc-color-base-200);
}
```

## 🎯 Theme Compatibility

### Automatic Theme Switching

Using Modus CSS variables ensures your components work with all 4 themes:

- **Classic Light** (default)
- **Classic Dark**
- **Modern Light**
- **Modern Dark**

### Testing Requirements

Always test your components with:

```tsx
export default function ThemeTest() {
  return (
    <div
      className="theme-test"
      style={{
        backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)",
        color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)",
      }}
    >
      {/* Your component here */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

Or with CSS Modules:

```tsx
import styles from "./ThemeTest.module.css";

export default function ThemeTest() {
  return <div className={styles.themeTest}>{/* Your component here */}</div>;
}
```

```css
/* ThemeTest.module.css */
.themeTest {
  /* Will automatically adapt to current theme */
  background-color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-page);
  color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-content);
}
```

